---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTASection from '@/components/CTASection.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '@/lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Golden Apple Export — Iranian Golden Delicious Wholesale | SibExport"
  description="Golden apple export from Iran. SibExport supplies Iranian golden apples wholesale to importers and distributors, graded and packed to specification. Request a quotation."
  path="/golden-apple-export/"
  ogImage="/images/golden-apple.png"
>
  <Breadcrumbs
    items={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Iranian Apple Varieties', href: '/iranian-apple-varieties/' },
      { label: 'Golden Apple Export' },
    ]}
  />
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Product"
    title="Golden apple export from Iran"
    description="Sweet, attractive golden apples sourced from Iranian orchards — carefully handled to preserve their pale color and flavor through export transit."
  />

  <article class="container-site py-14 lg:py-20">
    <div class="prose-site mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h2>The sweet side of the Iranian apple crop</h2>
      <p>
        Golden apples hold a distinctive place in wholesale apple trade.
        Their pale yellow color, smooth skin and honeyed sweetness set them
        apart from red and green categories, and in many markets they are a
        familiar favorite that customers reach for by name. In regional
        markets across the Middle East, Caucasus and beyond, golden apples
        are a staple of mixed wholesale programs — rarely the only apple a
        distributor buys, but almost always one of them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Iran's higher-elevation orchards, including those around Urmia in
        West Azerbaijan, produce golden apples with the sweetness and
        smooth appearance the category is known for. SibExport supplies
        golden apples for export in wholesale volumes, graded and packed
        against a specification agreed with each buyer before the order is
        confirmed.
      </p>

      <h3>Golden Delicious and the golden category</h3>
      <p>
        The best-known golden variety internationally is Golden Delicious,
        and Iran's orchards grow golden-type apples of this general profile:
        pale gold skin, crisp white flesh and a sweet, low-acid eating
        experience. Buyers searching for <em>Iranian Golden Delicious apples
        wholesale</em> should note that exact variety availability changes
        with the season — our practice is to discuss the season's actual crop
        with you and confirm in writing what your order will contain, rather
        than promise a variety list that storage and harvest timing may
        change.
      </p>

      <h3>Characteristics buyers care about</h3>

    <figure class="my-8">
      <img
        src="/images/golden-apple.svg"
        alt="Golden apples with smooth pale skin from Iranian orchards"
        width="1200"
        height="630"
        loading="lazy"
        class="w-full rounded-xl border border-border shadow-sm"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-muted-foreground">Golden apples with smooth pale skin from Iranian orchards</figcaption>
    </figure>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Color</strong> — the pale golden tone without green
          under-color that signals proper maturity for this category
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Skin condition</strong> — golden fruit shows handling marks
          more readily than darker apples, so careful picking and packing
          matter disproportionately
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sweetness</strong> — the high-sugar, low-acid profile that
          defines the category's eating quality
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Firmness retention</strong> — maintaining texture through
          transit, particularly for longer shipments
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Handling: why golden apples need extra care</h3>
      <p>
        There is a reason experienced importers ask pointed questions about
        how golden apples are handled. The fruit's thin, pale skin bruises
        more visibly than that of red varieties, and pressure marks that
        would be invisible on a dark red apple can down-grade a golden one.
        Quality in this category is largely decided at three moments: harvest
        timing, the care taken during picking and transfer, and the
        protective quality of interior packing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our golden apple supply follows the same sourcing and inspection
        discipline as the rest of our program, with particular attention to
        gentle handling and interior packaging that immobilizes the fruit.
        See our <a href="/apple-quality-specifications/">quality and
        specifications</a> approach and <a href="/apple-packaging/">packaging
        options</a> for the details.
      </p>

      <h3>Size counts and grading</h3>
      <p>
        As with all export apples, golden fruit is specified by count per
        carton combined with a grade setting tolerances for color, firmness
        and defects. Golden apples in wholesale trade often serve mixed
        programs — buyers who also purchase red and green categories
        frequently standardize counts across all three so their retail packs
        stay consistent. Tell us the count your market expects and we will
        confirm what the season's crop can deliver.
      </p>

      <h3>Packing and transportation</h3>
      <p>
        Golden apples ship in export-grade cartons with protective interior
        packaging. Because the category is more delicate than red fruit,
        packing specifications matter especially here: liner type, tray
        configuration and carton strength are all selected to match the
        length and conditions of the journey. Regional destinations reached
        by road — Iraq, the Caucasus, Turkey and the Gulf — keep transit
        short, which works strongly in the fruit's favor.
      </p>
      <p>
        Packing configuration, pallet layout and labeling are confirmed per
        order. For packing details, see <a href="/apple-packaging/">apple
        packaging for export</a>; for how an order moves from confirmation to
        loading, see the <a href="/apple-export-process/">export process</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Who this supply suits</h3>
      <p>
        Wholesale golden apples from Iran suit importers and distributors
        serving retail chains, produce markets and mixed-fruit programs. If
        your current supply of golden fruit is inconsistent — one shipment
        pale and mature, the next green and hard — a conversation about a
        written specification is the fix. Send us your requirements and we
        will respond with a realistic, tailored offer.
      </p>

      <h3>Frequently asked questions about golden apple supply</h3>
      <p><strong>Are Iranian Golden Delicious apples available in wholesale volumes?</strong><br />
      Golden-type apples are a regular part of Iran's commercial crop, and
      SibExport supplies the golden category in export volumes. Exact variety
      availability is confirmed per season against your specification.</p>
      <p><strong>How is the color requirement specified?</strong><br />
      Color expectations are written into the order specification — typically
      as the degree of ground color and absence of green — and checked at
      grading and loading.</p>
      <p><strong>Can golden apples be mixed with red and green in one program?</strong><br />
      Yes, mixed-class orders are common. Sizes and counts can be
      standardized across classes where the crop allows; confirm the details
      when requesting your quotation.</p>
      <p><strong>What is the minimum order quantity?</strong><br />
      MOQ depends on variety, packing and destination. Share your requirement
      and we will confirm the applicable minimum with your offer.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <CTASection
    title="Ready to buy Iranian golden apples?"
    description={`Send your sizes, counts, volume and destination — via the quotation form or WhatsApp at ${CONTACT.whatsappInternational} — for a tailored offer.`}
  />
</BaseLayout>
